The code in this directory is used to extract spectral data from X-Shooter and plots the data.


spec_extract.py
---------------
This code takes in the files downloaded from the ESO archive, and then splits it up for ease of use. 
It will first split the data up based on whether it is 'SCIENCE.SPECTRUM' (containing the wavelength
and flux data) or 'ANCILLARY.2DSPECTRUM' (containing flux measurement errors and quality flags). The
data is then split up based on object name. For 'SCIENCE.SPECTRUM', the data is further refined based
on if the data is 'UVB', 'VIS' or 'NIR'. The code will also plot the spectrum of each exposure as 
interactive .html files.
